# Commit after every completed run

When a Codex task in this repository finishes, immediately create a Git
checkpoint before ending the response:

```sh
git add -A
git commit -m "<concise description of what was fixed>"
```

Use a concise, accurate commit message describing the work completed in that
run. If no files changed, state that no commit was needed. Do not delay this
checkpoint until a later prompt.
